 "notes": "Spine: need -> gap -> P91 + zone-resolved method -> multipass weld -> PAG size || carbide dissolution (the two branches) -> MEC limited martensite -> transformation degree -> hardness gradient -> argued Type IV susceptibility -> conclusion. Audits: m22 (CGHAZ phase-map carbide density conflicts with dissolution; likely pseudo-indexing where KAM is highest) and m25 (no as-welded soft zone at the Type IV site, so the PRF claim rests on literature and PWHT expectations). Precipitate state typed with phase/fraction (dissolution), feature_size would carry coarsening, distribution carries placement: no precipitate leaf needed. Lost: BM baseline EBSD (F2,F3), F7 ICHAZ/BM border, F9/F11 maps (values used from text), F13 EDS image.",
 "migrated_from": "r03/graphs/Materials_Characterization__j.matchar.2016.05.024.json"
}